{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789235907,"nonce":"rdfbUjOyKB8VYfjcT7oaS9eW2JA=","title":"Key heap fiber-stack registrations by the u64 task id","message":"heap::gc_register_fiber_stack / gc_update_fiber_sp /\ngc_unregister_fiber_stack take a u32 id, inherited from ash where fiber\nids were u32. Scheduler task ids are u64 (krio TaskId), so a stackful\ntask registers its stack under the low 32 bits (sched/task.rs\nStackfulTask::gc_id). Unique until four billion tasks have been spawned in\none process, then two live stacks could share a key and one scan window\nwould be wrong.\n\nWiden the heap's fiber-stack table key to u64 and drop the truncation.\nash's seam passes u32 fiber ids (rt.rs gc_register_fiber_stack(id: u32,\n..)); the ash adapter widens on the way in, which is lossless.","files":null}]}